# Prose-budget ratchet baseline — issue #589.
#
# Files currently OVER their type budget in
# check-decomposition/thresholds.yml (bloat_thresholds). The gate fails a
# file above max(its type budget, its entry here), so these are frozen at
# their present size: they may shrink freely, and any growth fails.
#
# Regenerate with: tests/lint-prose-budget.sh --regen
# RAISING an entry is a deliberate, reviewable decision — a bigger file
# needs a reason in the commit message, not a silent regen.
#
# THE BUDGETS ARE TARGETS, NOT LAWS. Some files are genuinely better long. This
# file is the EXCEPTIONS LEDGER: each entry is consciously over budget, the
# ratchet stops it growing, and the trailing `#` note says WHY it is allowed.
# Add a rationale when you add an entry — --regen preserves existing ones, and
# the report lists any entry still missing one.
#
# Format: <repo-relative-path> <line-count> [# why this exception stands]
plugins/review-audit/agents/checker.md 580 # 7-step pipeline the pre-scan calls "mutually referential"; #503 moved the one separable block (Step 3a) to check-ai-config/agnix-prescan.md — further cuts tracked separately
plugins/workflow/skills/orchestrate/mode-protocol.md 877 # carries all orchestration modes; splitting per-mode would scatter one decision table an operator reads end-to-end
plugins/workflow/skills/ship-issue/ci-review-protocol.md 749 # the CI-wait + multi-cycle review contract; its length is the protocol, and every ship path loads it whole
